       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's double the usual maximum for metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (FDA labeling) and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould this be a typo? These are some common possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day), which is the max for immediate-release.\n- **1000 mg twice daily** (2,000 mg/day), a common target dose.\n- **1700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
