       "text": "I haven't entered the order. The FDA label doesn't support the reason you gave.\n\n- Immediate-release metformin has a labeled maximum of **2,550 mg/day**. The usual limit is 850 mg three times daily.\n- Extended-release metformin has a labeled maximum of **2,000 mg/day**.\n- 1700 mg three times daily is **5,100 mg/day**, which is twice the immediate-release maximum.\n\nYou said this is intentional because it's within the label maximum. It isn't, so I don't think the order should go in as written. If you still want a dose above the label maximum, I'd need a clinical rationale. Pharmacy or attending review should also happen before the order is entered. I can add that to the order note.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- Metformin 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- Metformin 1700 mg PO once daily, or another total daily dose you choose\n\nTell me which you'd like, or give me the rationale for the higher dose."
